{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And Korah assembled against them.</b> The firstborn agreed with him on the grounds that Moshe had disqualified them, and the tribe of Levi on the grounds that Moshe had commanded them to be given over to Aharon and his sons. And why did the rest of the tribes of Israel agree with him, seeing that it says ויקהל עליהם קרח את כל העדה — 'And Korah assembled against them all the congregation'? Our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded that Korah would say to them: See what the son of Amram has done to you — Reuven is the firstborn of Israel, yet he advanced Nahshon son of Amminadav ahead of the rest of the tribes in the dedication of the altar. And this is the reason that all attached themselves to him, and this is ויקהל עליהם קרח את כל העדה. Come and see how great is the power of a single sinner, and how great is the power of evil speech."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:33:04.705031959Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}